---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"profile\", \"switch\"])"
---
Switch the active profile live, with no reboot (needs the control channel of the gamepadii firmware). RAM only unless --save: the pad goes back to its saved profile when it restarts

Usage: gamepadii profile switch [OPTIONS] <PROFILE>

Arguments:
  <PROFILE>
          The profile: its number (1-6) or its label, any case

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --save
          Also save it to flash, as the profile hotkeys do

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
